Verdict: bug found

Line 28: `(void)p; observed=(int)strlen(text); return NULL;`

The reader does not participate in the writer’s protection discipline. strlen can inspect bytes while strcpy changes them; holding a lock only in the writer does not order the read.

| Step | Thread A | Thread B | Shared state |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | lock(m) succeeds |  | A owns m |
| 2 |  | strlen reads a text byte | B does not use m |
| 3 | strcpy writes a text byte |  | read/write conflict; C data race |

