answer:
Verdict: bug found

Line 24: `V(published);`
Line 25: `result=13;`

The post publishes only earlier actions. result is written afterward, so the consumer has no publication ordering for that write and may race with it.

| Step | Thread A | Thread B | Shared state |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | V(published) |  | permit available; result not filled |
| 2 |  | P(published) succeeds | B passed the publication point |
| 3 |  | read result | may precede or conflict with A’s later write |
| 4 | result=13 |  | write was not ordered before the read |

Fix:
```diff
--- prog.c
+++ prog.c (fixed)
@@ -21,8 +21,8 @@
 static int result;
 static void *a(void *p) {
     (void)p;
+    result=13;
     V(published);
-    result=13;
     return NULL;
 }
 static void *b(void *p) { (void)p; P(published); assert(result==13); return NULL; }
```

Complete the payload before signal(V), sem_post. A successful wait(P), sem_wait, then orders the consumer after that completed write.

