answer:
Verdict: bug found

Line 24: `V(gate);`
Line 25: `++web_count;`

Returning the permit before the critical section admits a second updater while the first still touches web_count.

| Step | Thread A | Thread B | Shared state |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | P(gate) succeeds |  | A owns the sole permit |
| 2 | V(gate) |  | gate available before update |
| 3 |  | P(gate) succeeds | B admitted |
| 4 | begin ordinary increment |  | A no longer excludes B |
| 5 |  | begin ordinary increment | conflicting accesses; C data race |

Fix:
```diff
--- prog.c
+++ prog.c (fixed)
@@ -21,8 +21,8 @@
 static int web_count;
 static void *a(void *p) {
     (void)p; P(gate);
+    ++web_count;
     V(gate);
-    ++web_count;
     return NULL;
 }
 static void *b(void *p) { return a(p); }
```

The exit signal(V) now follows the complete update. Each successful entry retains the unique permit throughout its ordinary increment.

