Verdict: bug found

Line 26: `if(i==0) continue;`

continue jumps past the exit section. The next loop entry attempts to reacquire the same normal mutex still owned by this worker.

| Step | Thread A | Thread B | Shared state |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | first iteration lock(m) succeeds |  | m=A |
| 2 | continue without unlocking |  | A still owns m |
| 3 | next iteration lock(m) blocks |  | self-deadlock on normal mutex |

Fix:
```diff
--- prog.c
+++ prog.c (fixed)
@@ -23,7 +23,7 @@
     (void)p;
     for(int i=0;i<2;i++) {
         ck(pthread_mutex_lock(&m));
-        if(i==0) continue;
+        if(i==0) { ck(pthread_mutex_unlock(&m)); continue; }
         ++processed; ck(pthread_mutex_unlock(&m));
     } return NULL;
