answer:
Verdict: bug found

Line 27: `(void)p; ck(pthread_rwlock_rdlock(&right)); ck(pthread_rwlock_wrlock(&left));`

Compatible read locks on different objects still form a cycle when each owner then seeks exclusive access to the other object [2].

| Step | Thread A | Thread B | Shared state |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | rdlock(left) succeeds |  | A holds left read |
| 2 |  | rdlock(right) succeeds | B holds right read |
| 3 | wrlock(right) blocks |  | B’s reader blocks A’s writer |
| 4 |  | wrlock(left) blocks | A’s reader blocks B’s writer |

